  $ flag b1.rebuilt
  $ do earn(-12)
  $ standing += 2
  $ humanity += 1
  $ collesanto += 1
  Pollio does not say anything. He draws the tablet toward him, and he writes a figure, and then, after a moment, another one under it that is a little smaller, and he looks up with a face from which something has gone quite suddenly out. "I shall have to find the timber," he says. "I have a man in Ostia. I will not pay him what he asks." He takes a breath. "I am very glad that you said it. I did not know how to." By the spring there are roofs on four of the lanes below the Esquiline, and over every door is a small neat sign painted by a man who was told not to, a six petaled flower, in a red that has not quite dried.
* Let the firm take the week's profit, and keep it quiet
  $ secrecy += 1
  $ humanity -= 1
  Pollio nods. He does it as he does everything, thoroughly. He writes the figure down and he locks the tablets in the chest. "It is only wise," he says, in a flat voice, "not to be seen to be generous this week." He says it as a man says a thing that has been said to him in an office. You say that you agree. You both know that it is not the only reason, and you do not discuss the other one.
